  "starterCode": "import pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_multi_column_selection(records: list, selected_columns: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Multi-Column Selection** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport pandas as pd\n\ndef pandas_multi_column_selection(records: list, selected_columns: list) -> list:\n    return pd.DataFrame(records)[selected_columns].to_dict(orient='records')\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
